        { "id": "draft-1-brief", "x": 0, "y": -230, "w": 460, "text": "Casomer Studio in the Carved Shell system — one page, six rows.\n\nRow 1: palette (the M4 gate) and the editor in its three viewport states. Row 2: the workspaces — page level, collection head-on, taxonomy terms, repeat. Row 3: template binding, picker, presence, discussion. Row 4: desktop surfaces and overlays. Row 5: onboarding. Row 6: moments — block seam, account, team publish (wrap up, then release), grace gate, supporter, delete.\n\nOne rule set ties it together: content in the tree, structure in the inspector, browsing in the workspace; amber is yours; unwrapped edits never publish; nothing deletes without naming its references." }
